 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nTonawanda city school district to establish an insurance reserve fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S1736",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1736-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1736\n\nSPONSOR: JACOBS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nTonawanda city school district to establish an insurance reserve fund\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would allow the Tonawanda City School District which has\nelected to self-insure to establish an insurance reserve fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1-Amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of § 6-n of the General Munic-\nipal Law by providing the Tonawanda City School District the ability to\nestablish an insurance reserve fund.\n\n§ 2-Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn order to prudently manage the rising costs of health insurance, the\nTonawanda City School District elected to self-insure its health benefit\nprogram. Self-insurance offers many advantages for school districts and\nits employees, however under current law school districts are prevented\nfrom retaining more than four percent of their budget in an unappropri-\nated fund balance. Authorizing the Tonawanda City School District to\nestablish an insurance reserve fund will allow them to manage year-to-\nyear variability in claims.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS. 8244 (2017-2018) Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
